# Data conversion between bit and megabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and megabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0000MB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0000MB; backward, converting 1MB to 8000000b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5MB yields 12000000.0b. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(MB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(MB))
backward_whole: int = 1MB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0000MB
0.0000MB
8000000b
12000000.0b

<<< stderr
